WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.120
- Welcome everyone today at
the bit of an unusual location,

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.390
we are in London, as I
guess you can see here

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:08.460
based on the buses.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.980
We are currently here on and
offsite with Building Radar.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.301
Next to me as Leopold,
who is managing director

00:00:13.301 --> 00:00:16.080
and founder of Building Radar.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.060
he is also former school friend of mine,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.550
worked at Google among
other companies before.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.220
So looking forward now to
go actually to a WeWork

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.350
to meet a couple of other colleagues

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.850
from the Building Radar team.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:30.090
We have a little team that
is based here in London.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.260
I trust we are going to spend

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.900
a few very productive,
insightful days here.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.029
And I will bring you along
of what is happening,

00:00:36.029 --> 00:00:37.560
what we are doing.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.420
So we are on our way to the WeWork,

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.990
actually love the city
because I spent one year here

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:45.000
at London School of
Economics, for a master.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.520
And at the WeWork, our
chief product officer

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.283
was already waiting for us.

00:00:49.283 --> 00:00:52.410
WeWorks are I think always
an interesting experience

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.060
some pros and cons of working

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.610
in a co-working space like that.

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.199
For our use case it definitely
was great to sit together

00:00:59.199 --> 00:01:01.530
with some colleague of us.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:04.740
We were one of the first people
here in the WeWork today.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.900
At lunch, we went to Chinatown.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.970
I always love the Chinatown in London,

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.880
this vibrant radiating atmosphere.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.520
A good friend of us who
is also Chinese background

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.640
recommended us a really nice lunch place.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.810
It was amazing food and
actually also quiet affordable

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.480
so definitely very much worth attending.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.400
So afterwards we had some additional time

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.840
to explore the area.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.240
My wife was actually with me as well,

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.130
together with our baby girl.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:35.580
Actually later this year we
are expecting our second baby,

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.840
our second child, so exciting
times for us, for sure.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:41.970
And afterwards we headed
back to the WeWork

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.257
to get some additional work done.

00:01:43.257 --> 00:01:46.980
We were debating some new
features that we want to launch

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.020
for Building Radar platform,

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.900
realized that we all have
slightly different ideas

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.270
of how these were supposed to look like

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.940
so we figured let's just
take a sheet of paper,

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:00.210
let's just draw down
what we have in our minds

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:01.590
to then compare this.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.210
Think this was quite
an effective exercise.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:07.350
This time, We also moved
to slightly different area

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:11.010
of the WeWork which was
a little bit quieter.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.230
We were a little bit more for ourselves.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:16.650
And this led to, I think,
a quite productive session

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:19.200
with lots of ideation happening together

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.930
with our London-based colleagues.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.420
Afterwards, we did something
that I missed quite a lot

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:27.300
and this is enjoying
the London pub culture.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.910
So we met at one of the
traditional London pubs,

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.350
enjoyed a nice beer

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.440
and had just a very good time in general.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:37.090
After that, of course,
we also visited LSE,

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.630
London School of Economics university,

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.280
where I did my master.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.710
They did upgrade the university facilities

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.620
quite significantly since I was there.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.420
Then the other day we went back there

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.548
just also to explore the campus by day.

00:02:50.548 --> 00:02:53.130
Currently graduations were going on.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:57.690
So congrats to everyone who
recently graduated from LSE.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.370
I found the academic experience

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:00.990
to be reasonably challenging,

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:04.560
so this is definitely
very, very much deserved.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.680
In the master program, I focused
on accounting and finance

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.180
and the knowledge that I acquired

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.310
during this year definitely helped me

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:14.220
on almost every single project afterwards

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.440
in consulting at McKinsey, so for me,

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.570
this experience was definitely worth it.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.790
And also quite a lot of fun, indeed.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.160
Afterwards, we were invited by
some friends who are working

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.740
as barristers in London to have lunch

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:29.700
at a very special location,
definitely enjoyed this one.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.590
And then the next day, on the weekend

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:33.510
we went to some parks in London.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.910
This is Piccadilly circus,
actually very close

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:39.660
to where the McKinsey office
at least used to be in London.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.100
We had an amazing time.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.230
There are some areas in
London where you feel like

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.060
you're actually not in London at all,

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.890
but that seemed to be more like Munich

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:48.180
or someplace like that.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:49.770
So definitely enjoyed myself

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.900
also being there with my family.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.110
And then afterwards we also
had the opportunity to visit

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:56.760
a good friend who lived

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:59.910
in the new Battersea
real estate development.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:02.400
This is a very new real
estate development project

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:06.390
with some amazing living units
that are being created there.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.940
Also completely different experience

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.160
compared to what you're
usually used to in London.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.930
I hope you enjoyed these impressions.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:14.490
Leave a like if you did.

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.650
Big, big thanks to all
the members as well.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.020
My name is Heinrich,
releasing weekly content.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.220
See you again next week.

